{"context":"eka status today is workspace-global (shows 7 projects regardless of cwd). Users working inside a repository expect repo-local relevance. Execution state currently lives in .eka/execution-state.md (git-ignored, not canonical, not synced) — separate ADR 037 covers its CKO migration. This ADR decides the status scoping contract so status can later surface the execution-state CKO as 'current state only'. Validated: derives-from eka/req:eka-improvements, dimension decisions, strata 2, approved via Gate 4 self-review (qa/code-review/product-review PASS) + user confirmation 2026-09-06.","decision":"When eka status runs inside an EKA repository (eka.yaml present + registered + synced), it shows only that repository's project + its repos and their last syncs (repo-scoped projection). Outside any repo, it keeps global behavior. Add --all flag to force global even inside a repo. Add --json machine output for scripts. MCP status tool mirrors same rule. Status surfaces execution-state CKO's current snapshot (latest instanceVersion) — not full history — via a new 'Execution' section. Scope resolution: detect cwd repo via eka.yaml lookup (same as eka view), filter WorkspaceStatus to that project/repo, emit global if none found.","consequences":"Positive: noise reduction, per-repo relevance, aligns with project-union model, enables cross-device consistency. Negative: breaking change for scripts — mitigated by --all + --json. Neutral: MCP parity required.","alternativesConsidered":"1) Client-only render filter in cmd/status.go; 2) Workspace.Status(repoFilter) server-side param with MCP parity; 3) Flag-only --repo/--project without auto-detection; 4) Hybrid auto-scoped + --all override (chosen).","status":"accepted"}